      "score": 15,
      "comments": 16,
      "author": "caius",
      "published": "2026-08-10T11:41:16Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Focus on low-level systems programming, language experimentation, and developing specialized command-line developer tooling.",
        "Allocate engineering cycles toward refactoring legacy codebases, resolving technical debt, and optimizing build pipeline performance.",
        "Leverage asynchronous developer communities to track open-source maintenance, architectural experiments, and peer project updates."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "security",
      "title": "Exploiting System Management Mode with a very long interrupt",
      "url": "https://github.com/xoreaxeaxeax/smiiiiiiiiiiiiiiii",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49245491",
      "score": 152,
      "comments": 55,
      "author": "WhiteDawn",
      "published": "2026-08-10T16:03:14Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Extended interrupt delays exploit race conditions in x86 System Management Interrupt (SMI) handlers to corrupt firmware state during execution.",
        "Attackers with Ring 0 access can leverage timing vulnerabilities to achieve arbitrary code execution in Ring -2 (SMM).",
        "Mitigation requires vendor firmware patches, strict SMI handler validation, and enforcing hardware-level timing constraints on interrupt processing."
      ]
    },
    {
