      "bullets": [
        "Ross Scott's 'Stop Killing Games' movement advocates for legal mandates requiring publishers to leave games in a playable state post-support.",
        "The initiative targets live-service shutdowns like Ubisoft's The Crew, pushing for regulatory requirements on server binaries and offline patches.",
        "Future game architecture may require built-in end-of-life plans, including dedicated self-hosting capabilities and decoupled online authentication systems."
